description:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set a new pulse for healthcare!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an &lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to join the &lt;strong&gt;Scheduling&lt;/strong&gt; team in &lt;strong&gt;Berlin&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission will be to give practitioners their day back:&amp;nbsp; reclaiming the admin time they spend creating and managing appointments, so care teams can focus on what matters. You will work in a feature team developing scheduling infrastructure and booking experiences, contributing directly to a platform that books billions of appointments a year for health professionals and patients across Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in the tech team at Doctolib means building innovative products and features to improve the daily lives of care teams and patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities include but are not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead a team of 6 to 7 engineers&lt;/strong&gt; of mixed seniority, owning delivery, quality and production health end to end — keeping engagement high and standards higher&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Together with your product partner, define the mission and vision for your team and build a roadmap you can defend to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in architecture reviews and help shape the technical direction of the Scheduling stream, including the migration of core scheduling capabilities from the monolith into purpose-built services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and uphold the security, reliability, performance and scalability standards required to remain the most trusted e-health SaaS in Europe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Talent and People teams to recruit, develop and retain engineers through career conversations and feedback they can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed AI-assisted engineering into how your team works day to day, with a clear and honest view of where it helps and where it does not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve how the team operates — planning, on-call, bug backlog, incident follow-up — so the team spends its energy on what moves the needle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before you read on: if you don&#39;t have the exact profile described below, but you feel this job description matches your skill set, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be a great fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have at least &lt;strong&gt;6 years&lt;/strong&gt; of software engineering experience and &lt;strong&gt;3 years&lt;/strong&gt; of engineering management experience, including leading a team of 5+ engineers through delivery, hiring and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are credible with senior backend engineers — distributed systems, data modelling, latency and throughput are conversations you can hold and challenge; you stay close enough to the code to review a pull request, without needing to be the one writing it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience &lt;strong&gt;modernising a large legacy system&lt;/strong&gt;, ideally extracting services from a monolith, and know how to keep a team delivering while the ground moves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are an effective communicator who can translate company goals into team objectives, and who says the uncomfortable thing early rather than late&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think critically and objectively, with a solution-oriented approach that brings people with you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It would be fantastic if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked in a regulated industry such as healthcare or fintech, where privacy and data protection shape design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have navigated hyper-growth environments and understand the trade-offs they force on architecture and team organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have formed a considered view on AI coding assistants — their real benefits and their real shortcomings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Doctolib Tech&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our solutions are built on a single fully cloud-native platform that supports web and mobile app interfaces, multiple languages, and is adapted to country and healthcare specialty requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our stack in this product area is Ruby on Rails and TypeScript/React in the monolith, Kotlin for new services, with Postgres, Redis and Kafka underneath.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We leverage AI ethically across our products to empower patients and health professionals. Discover our AI vision &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.doctolib.com/ai-careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
